/*!
\page page_stepdcollection StEpdCollection — Collection Documentation

\section epd_overview Overview

\ref StEpdCollection is the event-level container for hits in the
<b>Event Plane Detector (EPD)</b>.

The EPD is a pair of scintillator-tile wheels at forward rapidity
(2.14 < |η| < 5.09) — one on each side of the STAR interaction point.
Each wheel has 12 supersectors × 31 tiles, read out via SiPMs and QT boards.
It provides high-multiplicity forward signals used for event-plane determination,
centrality estimation, and ZDC-SMD cross-calibration.

One \ref StEpdHit is created for each tile that registers a valid signal.

\section epd_ownership Object Ownership

- <b>mEpdHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecEpdHit): Owned; \c StSPtrVec deletes elements on
  destruction.  The \ref StEpdCollection destructor is a <b>no-op</b>; cleanup is
  handled by \c StSPtrVec and the \c StEvent framework.

\section epd_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecEpdHit | mEpdHits | Collection of \ref StEpdHit objects — one per good tile hit. Each stores: tile ID (supersector 1–12, tile 1–31, east/west side ±1), QT ADC, TDC, TAC values, TAC presence flag, gain-corrected energy loss in MIP MPV units, and database quality flag. |

\section epd_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c epdHits() | Reference to the EPD hit collection (mutable and const overloads). |
| \c addHit(const StEpdHit*) | Appends an EPD tile hit (null-safe). |
| \c hitsPresent() const | Returns \c true if at least one hit is present. |

\section epd_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StEpdCollection* epdColl = event->epdCollection();
if (!epdColl || !epdColl->hitsPresent()) return;

const StSPtrVecEpdHit& hits = epdColl->epdHits();
for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
    StEpdHit* hit = hits[i];
    int   position = hit->position();  // supersector 1-12
    int   tile     = hit->tile();      // tile 1-31
    int   side     = hit->side();      // +1 West, -1 East
    float nMIP     = hit->nMIP();      // gain-calibrated energy loss in MIP units
    bool  good     = hit->isGood();    // database quality flag
}
\endcode

\see StEpdHit
*/
